00 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56313"} "400 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56338"} "800 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56349"} "1,500 metres, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56360"} "5 miles, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56369"} "Marathon, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56370"} "110 metres Hurdles, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56392"} "400 metres Hurdles, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56432"} "1,600 metres Medley Relay, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56438"} "3 miles, Team, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56421"} "3,500 metres Race Walk, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56427"} "10 miles Race Walk, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56443"} "High Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56454"} "Standing High Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56461"} "Pole Vault, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56467"} "Long Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56475"} "Standing Long Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56482"} "Triple Jump, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56488"} "Shot Put, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56495"} "Discus Throw, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56504"} "Discus Throw, Greek Style, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56511"} "Hammer Throw, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56517"} "Javelin Throw, Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "56522"} "Javelin Throw, Freestyle, Men"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:span {} "Not held in other editions"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/55"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "3,200 metres Steeplechase, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "17 – 18 July 1908"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/216"} "White City Stadium, London"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/56412"} "24 from 6 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Steeplechase racing was mostly popular in Great Britain, although steeplechase events had been on the Olympic programme in both 1900 and 1904.  But, because the event was not held frequently outside of Britain, it was difficult to consider any challenger other than the British runners.  The last five AAA titles in steeplechase had been won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/69456"} "Arthur Russell"] " (1904-06), " [:a {:href "/athletes/69039"} "Joe English"] " (1907), and Reginald Noakes (1908).  Noakes would later win the 1909 and 1911 AAA titles, and English won again in 1910.  English competed at the 1908 Olympics but did not finish the second heat.  Noakes did not compete due to injury."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Four Britons, one American, and one Canadian qualified for the final.  A notable non-qualifier was " [:a {:href "/athletes/78697"} "Jim Lightbody"] " (USA), the " [:a {:href "/results/56139"} "1904 Olympic champion"] ", who finished second to " [:a {:href "/athletes/69474"} "Harry Sewell"] " in heat six.  In the final, at the bell, Arthur Russell, " [:a {:href "/athletes/69442"} "Arthur Robertson"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/78366"} "John Eisele"] " were together.  Halfway through the last lap, Robertson took the lead, and Eisele was dropped with 220 yards remaining.  Russell passed Robertson at the water jump and held on to win by 2 yards.  Eisele did well to finish third, as in training he had torn away a toe-nail and it was not certain he would compete."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69456"} "Arthur Russell"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "10:56.2 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "10:47.8 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold